# Trivy ignore list — base-OS CVEs in the RUNTIME image base
# gcr.io/distroless/nodejs22-debian13:nonroot (Debian 13 "trixie"), i.e. what
# `trivy image` actually scans (the node:26-slim build stage is not shipped).
# Every entry is an ACCEPTED, DOCUMENTED risk with no runtime path in our Node-only proto
# server (distroless: no shell, no perl, nothing but node + libs). Most also have NO fixed
# version available in trixie — literally nothing to bump to. The exception is the last
# group (openssl QUIC/CMP/CMS/DTLS/RPK, added 2026-08-26): a fix EXISTS in Debian but has
# not reached the distroless base, which ships no package manager to install it with.
# That distinction decides the exit: "no fix" entries wait on Debian, "fix not in the base
# yet" entries wait on an upstream rebuild — and die with it.
# Each is an accepted, documented risk; re-review whenever the base image digest
# is bumped (SEC-1 baseline discipline; ties to audit SD-5.1 / F-15).
#
# Reviewed 2026-07-10 (SEC-1): previous entries (bookworm perl/ncurses/zlib-minizip
# from the old node:22-slim single-stage image) no longer apply to the distroless
# runtime and were removed after the trivy-image scan came back to life (the
# corepack build break had silently disabled it — caught by the SEC-1 gate).
#
# Reviewed 2026-08-11 (SEC-22): +2 glibc wordexp entries below. The rest were re-checked
# against the same base image digest and all still apply.
#
# Reviewed 2026-08-17: +1 libssl3t64 QUIC-server entry below. Same base image digest,
# so the earlier entries were not re-verified individually this time.
#
# Reviewed 2026-08-20: +1 libssl3t64 EVP_Cipher/AEAD entry below (CVE-2026-75803). Same
# base image digest again, so the earlier entries were not re-verified individually.
#
# Reviewed 2026-08-26 (AI-BAL-4 CI): +1 libc6 strfmon entry below (CVE-2026-19499). Тот же
# сценарий, что у SEC-24/SEC-25: находка пришла в ленту Trivy МЕЖДУ прогонами — последний
# `main` (13:35 UTC, мерж #809) был зелёным, а прогон в 14:01 уже красный, — и, поскольку
# `trivy image` работает без --severity, одна MEDIUM-строка закрывает очередь всем веткам
# сразу. Дифф PR при этом не касался ни базы, ни Dockerfile, ни зависимостей.
#
# Reviewed 2026-08-24 (SEC-24): +1 libc6 tdelete entry below (CVE-2026-19542). The FIRST
# review at which the base image digest actually MOVED: the `nonroot` tag stopped resolving
# to the sha256:939d6f16… then pinned in the Dockerfile and moved to sha256:22d2f048…. That
# rebuild is NOT a remediation — both images ship the same libc6 2.41-12+deb13u3, libssl3t64
# 3.5.6-1~deb13u2 and zlib1g 1:1.3.dfsg+really1.3.1-1+b1 (read straight out of
# /var/lib/dpkg/status.d in both amd64 manifests, pulled from gcr.io on 2026-08-24).
#
# Reviewed 2026-08-26 (SEC-25): the pin was bumped to that rebuilt base
# (sha256:22d2f048…, still what `nonroot` resolves to on this date) and EVERY entry below
# was re-verified against it, individually, for the first time since 2026-08-11 — the
# review the 08-17 and 08-20 notes deferred. Package versions were read out of
# /var/lib/dpkg/status.d in the new image's amd64 manifest (pulled from gcr.io on
# 2026-08-26): libssl3t64 3.5.6-1~deb13u2, libc6 2.41-12+deb13u3, zlib1g
# 1:1.3.dfsg+really1.3.1-1+b1 — identical to the old base, so the bump closes NO entry
# here and none was removed. Wording that said "the tag still resolves to the pinned
# sha256:939d6f16…" was stale on the digit and has been corrected in place.
# +8 libssl3t64 entries below (openssl QUIC/CMP/CMS/DTLS/RPK). Those are the first
# suppressions in this file that are NOT of the "nothing to bump to" kind: Debian HAS
# published a fix (3.5.7-1~deb13u2) — it simply has not reached the distroless base yet,
# and distroless has no package manager to upgrade it in. That makes them the shortest-
# lived entries here: they go away with the next upstream rebuild, and are to be REMOVED
# then, not extended.

# libc6 2.41-12+deb13u3 — MEDIUM, no fixed version published for trixie yet.
CVE-2026-5435
CVE-2026-5450
CVE-2026-5928
CVE-2026-6238

# libc6 — ancient LOW, disputed/won't-fix upstream (Debian marks them minor/unimportant),
# no fixed version; carried by every glibc-based image.
CVE-2010-4756
CVE-2018-20796
CVE-2019-1010022
CVE-2019-1010023
CVE-2019-1010024
CVE-2019-1010025
CVE-2019-9192

# zlib1g 1:1.3.dfsg+really1.3.1-1+b1 — MEDIUM, no fixed version for trixie.
CVE-2026-27171

# libc6 2.41-12+deb13u3 — LOW, both in glibc's wordexp(): CVE-2026-6368 (calling wordexp
# with WRDE_APPEND returns uninitialized memory, a later wordfree may abort the process),
# CVE-2026-6791 (expanding a path that begins with «~username»). Published to the feed
# between 2026-08-10 and 2026-08-11 and, because `trivy image` runs without --severity,
# these two LOW findings alone closed the merge queue for the whole repository.
# Not reachable here: the runtime is distroless (no shell) and the server is Node —
# wordexp()/wordfree() is a C API for shell-style word expansion that neither our code
# nor the Node runtime calls. No fix as of this review: re-checked on 2026-08-26 against
# the rebuilt base now pinned in the Dockerfile (sha256:22d2f048…) — same libc6
# 2.41-12+deb13u3, still no fixed version for trixie. Re-review at the next digest bump.
CVE-2026-6368
CVE-2026-6791

# libssl3t64 3.5.6-1~deb13u2 — MEDIUM, Debian status `fix_deferred` (no fixed version).
# OpenSSL flaw on the QUIC SERVER path ("When an OpenSSL QUIC server (Listener SSL object)
# proce…"). Not reachable here: this image serves HTTP/1.1 + WebSocket over TCP (Fastify,
# `packages/server/src/wsServer.ts` builds an http.Server — or an https.Server when RS-5.1
# native TLS is configured, still TLS-over-TCP), never QUIC/HTTP-3; in the deployed stack
# TLS is normally terminated by Caddy in front. Node exposes no OpenSSL QUIC listener API,
# and the runtime is distroless — no shell and no `openssl` CLI to reach it another way.
# No fix to bump to: re-checked on 2026-08-26 against the newly pinned base
# (sha256:22d2f048…) — it still ships libssl3t64 3.5.6-1~deb13u2, and Debian still carries
# this one as `fix_deferred`, so there is no fixed version anywhere to bump to.
# Re-review when the digest is bumped again or Debian publishes a fix.
CVE-2026-14456

# libssl3t64 3.5.6-1~deb13u2 — severity UNKNOWN (the feed carries no score yet), and
# "(no fixed version)". OpenSSL, "Check the tag on EVP_Cipher() finalize: Poly1305 and
# OCB AEADs": on the finalize path of the one-shot AEAD API the authentication tag could
# go unchecked.
# Reached the feed AFTER the last green `main` run (2026-08-19 15:50 UTC, security-scan
# run 2716), so it is not something a PR introduced: it turned `trivy image` red on every
# branch at once, and the next weekly run will redden `main` itself. Because the scan runs
# without --severity, this single unscored row closes the merge queue for the whole repo.
# Suppressed NOT because the finding was judged harmless, but because there is nothing to
# fix: no fixed libssl3t64 is published for trixie for THIS CVE, and the rebuilt base now
# pinned in the Dockerfile (sha256:22d2f048…, re-read from gcr.io on 2026-08-26) ships the
# same libssl3t64 3.5.6-1~deb13u2 — so there is still nothing to bump to.
# What was verified directly: neither our packages nor the prototype use ChaCha20-Poly1305
# or OCB (no `createCipheriv` and no mention of those ciphers anywhere in the tree), and
# the runtime is distroless — no shell, no `openssl` CLI; in the deployed stack TLS is
# normally terminated by Caddy in front. What could NOT be verified: the advisory text
# itself (security-tracker.debian.org and avd.aquasec.com are unreachable from the dev
# environment), so a path through OpenSSL's own ChaCha20-Poly1305 TLS ciphersuite cannot
# be ruled out. The risk is therefore accepted for a SHORT window, not open-endedly.
# Re-review 2026-09-03 — or sooner, as soon as Debian publishes a fix or the base image
# digest is bumped. If a fix appears, this entry is REMOVED, not extended.
CVE-2026-75803

# libc6 2.41-12+deb13u3 — severity UNKNOWN (Debian has not scored it) and "(no fixed
# version)". glibc, "Out-of-bounds stack array access in tdelete" — the POSIX binary-search-
# tree API (<search.h>: tsearch/tfind/tdelete/twalk).
# `main` went red WITHOUT a code change, and this time that is provable without a re-run:
# the very same commit 671c03f6 was scanned GREEN by the push run 32628248009 (2026-08-23
# 08:26 UTC) and RED by the weekly scheduled run 32695151718 (2026-08-24 05:53 UTC). Only
# the CVE feed moved between them — which is exactly what the weekly re-scan of `main`
# exists to catch. Because `trivy image` runs without --severity, this single unscored row
# closed the merge queue for the whole repository again (#777, a docs-only PR, was the one
# left blocked).
# Suppressed NOT because the finding was judged harmless, but because there is nothing to
# fix: no fixed libc6 is published for trixie (Trivy's Fixed Version column is empty), and
# the rebuilt base image does not carry one either — see the 2026-08-24 review note above.
# What was verified directly: nothing in this repo uses the tsearch/tdelete family (it is a
# C API, and there is no reference to it anywhere in packages/ or prototype/), and the
# runtime is distroless — no shell, no C tooling to reach it another way. What could NOT be
# verified: the advisory text itself (security-tracker.debian.org, api.osv.dev and
# avd.aquasec.com are all blocked by the dev environment's egress proxy), so a glibc-
# INTERNAL caller of tdelete cannot be ruled out from here. The risk is therefore accepted
# for a SHORT window, not open-endedly.
# Re-review 2026-09-07 — or sooner, as soon as Debian publishes a fix. If a fix appears,
# this entry is REMOVED, not extended.
CVE-2026-19542

# libssl3t64 3.5.6-1~deb13u2 — 3×MEDIUM + 5×LOW, and the FIRST group in this file with a
# published fix: Debian ships 3.5.7-1~deb13u2 (Trivy's "Fixed Version" column, unlike every
# entry above). It is suppressed anyway because we cannot install it: the runtime is
# distroless — the base image IS the package set, there is no apt/apk to upgrade inside it,
# and the rebuilt base pinned in the Dockerfile (sha256:22d2f048…) still carries 3.5.6-1~deb13u2
# (read from /var/lib/dpkg/status.d in its amd64 manifest, pulled from gcr.io on 2026-08-26).
# So the fix is real, reachable only by an upstream distroless rebuild, and not by us.
#
# Why this closed the merge queue: the finding reached the feed after the last green `main`
# push run (2026-08-25 21:02 UTC) and, because `trivy image` runs without --severity, all 8
# rows — 5 of them LOW — turned the blocking job red on every branch at once, including 8
# dependabot PRs and #803.
#
# Not reachable here, protocol by protocol — none of these code paths exists in this image:
#   · QUIC (CVE-2026-18798 server INITIAL-packet double free, CVE-2026-63075 ACK-only packet
#     retention → memory exhaustion): the server is HTTP/1.1 + WebSocket over TCP (Fastify
#     `http.Server`, or `https.Server` under RS-5.1 native TLS — still TLS-over-TCP). Node's
#     QUIC binding is behind `--experimental-quic`, and the image's CMD passes no such flag.
#   · CMP — Certificate Management Protocol (CVE-2026-63076 invalid pointer deref via crafted
#     protectionAlg, CVE-2026-63073 sender DN used as format string, CVE-2026-63074 ExtraCerts
#     cache growth): Node exposes no CMP API at all, and nothing here speaks it.
#   · CMS — Cryptographic Message Syntax (CVE-2026-63072 heap overflow in key unwrapping):
#     likewise unexposed by Node; no PKCS#7/CMS anywhere in the tree.
#   · DTLS (CVE-2026-54874 memory buffering records for a future epoch): no datagram TLS —
#     verified by grep, the tree has no DTLS and no UDP transport.
#   · RPK — RFC 7250 raw public keys (CVE-2026-14457 signature-algorithm selection can
#     dereference a missing certificate): not enabled; the server presents ordinary X.509.
# And, as for every entry above, the runtime is distroless: no shell and no `openssl` CLI to
# reach any of it another way.
#
# What could NOT be verified: the advisory texts themselves — security-tracker.debian.org and
# avd.aquasec.com are blocked by the dev environment's egress proxy, so the reachability
# argument rests on the protocol each CVE names (from Trivy's own titles) plus this repo's
# code, not on reading upstream's analysis. The risk is therefore accepted for a SHORT window.
# Re-review 2026-09-02 — or sooner, the moment the distroless base is rebuilt with
# 3.5.7-1~deb13u2. When it is, this whole group is REMOVED, not extended: unlike the entries
# above, it has a fix waiting, and a suppression outliving its fix is exactly the debt this
# file's discipline exists to prevent.
CVE-2026-18798
CVE-2026-63072
CVE-2026-63076
CVE-2026-14457
CVE-2026-54874
CVE-2026-63073
CVE-2026-63074
CVE-2026-63075

# --- 2026-08-26, libc6 strfmon (AI-BAL-4 CI) -------------------------------------------
# CVE-2026-19499 — libc6 2.41-12+deb13u3, MEDIUM, "glibc: Buffer Overflow in strfmon
# right-justification padding". Fixed Version в отчёте ПУСТ: исправления для trixie ещё нет,
# бампать нечего — это ожидание Debian, а не нашей сборки.
#
# Почему недостижимо здесь, и это ПРОВЕРЕНО, а не выведено из общих соображений:
#   · `strfmon()`/`strfmon_l()` — POSIX-форматирование ДЕНЕЖНЫХ величин по локали, C API.
#     Её надо вызвать явно из нативного кода; из JS к ней хода нет.
#   · Единственный потребитель libc в этом образе — сам `node` (runtime distroless: ни
#     шелла, ни утилит, ни пакетного менеджера). Проверка на бинарнике той же мажорной
#     версии: `nm -D $(command -v node) | grep strfmon` — пусто, и `strings` не находит
#     символа вовсе. Node её не импортирует и не может позвать.
#   · Денежное форматирование в JS (`Intl.NumberFormat` со `style: 'currency'`) реализовано
#     в ICU поверх данных CLDR — оно не ходит в локали glibc и не трогает strfmon.
#   · В нашем коде нативных аддонов нет: сервер — чистый JS (Fastify + ws), сборка не
#     компилирует C/C++ (`pnpm install --ignore-scripts` в образе).
#
# Что НЕ удалось проверить: текст самого advisory — security-tracker.debian.org и
# avd.aquasec.com закрыты egress-прокси среды разработки, как и в прошлый раз. Аргумент
# опирается на заголовок находки (функция названа прямо) плюс проверку бинарника, а не на
# чтение анализа апстрима.
#
# Re-review 2026-09-02 — вместе с openssl-группой выше, одним заходом. Как только Debian
# выпустит исправленный libc6 и distroless-база будет пересобрана, запись УДАЛЯЕТСЯ.
CVE-2026-19499

# --- 2026-08-27, libc6 SHIFT_JISX0213 (BAL-8 CI) ---------------------------------------
# CVE-2026-77117 — libc6 2.41-12+deb13u3, MEDIUM, "glibc: Non-progress DoS in
# SHIFT_JISX0213". Fixed Version в отчёте ПУСТ: исправления для trixie нет, бампать нечего.
# Тот же сценарий, что у CVE-2026-19499 и CVE-2026-19542: находка пришла в ленту Trivy
# между прогонами, дифф PR (JSON игрового контента + карта прототипа) не касался ни базы,
# ни Dockerfile, ни зависимостей, а `trivy image` работает без --severity, поэтому одна
# MEDIUM-строка закрывает очередь мержа всем веткам сразу.
#
# Почему недостижимо здесь — ПРОВЕРЕНО на бинарнике той же мажорной версии (node v22):
#   · SHIFT_JISX0213 — конвертер японской кодировки внутри glibc'шного iconv. Чтобы до него
#     дойти, нужно позвать `iconv_open("SHIFT_JISX0213", …)` из нативного кода.
#   · `nm -D --undefined-only $(command -v node) | grep -E 'iconv_open|iconv_close|iconv'` —
#     ПУСТО: node не импортирует ни одного символа glibc iconv. `strings` не находит в
#     бинарнике и самой строки `SHIFT_JISX0213`.
#   · Перекодировки в Node (`TextDecoder('shift_jis')` и прочее) обслуживает ВСТРОЕННЫЙ ICU
#     поверх данных CLDR (сборка с полным ICU: `process.config.variables.icu_small === false`),
#     а не локали glibc. Имена вроде `shift_jis` в бинарнике — это ICU-алиасы, не конвертеры
#     glibc.
#   · Единственный потребитель libc в образе — сам `node`: рантайм distroless, ни шелла, ни
#     утилит, ни пакетного менеджера. Нативных аддонов у нас нет (сервер — чистый JS, сборка
#     идёт с `--ignore-scripts`).
#
# Что НЕ удалось проверить: текст самого advisory — security-tracker.debian.org и
# avd.aquasec.com закрыты egress-прокси среды разработки. Аргумент опирается на заголовок
# находки (конвертер назван прямо) плюс проверку бинарника, а не на чтение анализа апстрима.
#
# Re-review 2026-09-02 — вместе с openssl-группой и strfmon, одним заходом. Как только Debian
# выпустит исправленный libc6 и distroless-база будет пересобрана, запись УДАЛЯЕТСЯ.
CVE-2026-77117
